1
00:00:11,022 --> 00:00:15,943
TRAGEDY ON THE WAVES

2
00:00:16,527 --> 00:00:19,113
[male staff] Jeez,
just look at all this blood.

3
00:00:19,655 --> 00:00:22,658
If he were anyone else,
I don't think he'd come back here.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,118
[male staff groans]

5
00:00:24,952 --> 00:00:28,414
[slowly] There, now you have

6
00:00:28,497 --> 00:00:32,126
some more melon leaves.

7
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:35,004
[Legoshi] <i>He's still talking to Melon.</i>

8
00:00:35,087 --> 00:00:39,091
[male staff] I swear, if I have to carry
another dead body out of this place...

9
00:00:39,175 --> 00:00:41,093
So, what do you plan on getting today?

10
00:00:41,177 --> 00:00:44,346
What? Oh, uh... [chuckles]
I mean, I would pick...

11
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:47,558
[laughs] I think black bunny there
would look good on you.

12
00:00:47,641 --> 00:00:49,226
{\an8}[Legoshi] Huh? Oh.

13
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:53,564
{\an8}<i>Miss Cosmo mentioned a strange pattern.
Could this be it?</i>

14
00:00:54,148 --> 00:00:57,443
{\an8}[Holger] They suit you better than...

15
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,905
the leopard spots.

16
00:01:02,364 --> 00:01:05,618
Are you afraid?

17
00:01:05,701 --> 00:01:09,038
[Legoshi] <i>What if Melon is transforming</i>

18
00:01:10,122 --> 00:01:11,540
<i>the way my mom did?</i>

19
00:01:12,541 --> 00:01:16,420
- Are you anxious?
- Huh?

20
00:01:17,004 --> 00:01:22,092
- You must feel so alone.
- Hmm.

21
00:01:22,176 --> 00:01:29,141
I guess you have always been alone.

22
00:01:29,225 --> 00:01:30,392
[Legoshi] <i>That's right.</i>

23
00:01:31,435 --> 00:01:33,896
<i>I thought he was a being of pure evil,</i>

24
00:01:34,814 --> 00:01:36,690
<i>but he's still just like anyone else.</i>

25
00:01:37,525 --> 00:01:41,821
If only someone out there

26
00:01:41,904 --> 00:01:47,034
was able to truly understand you.

27
00:01:47,118 --> 00:01:48,661
- [male staff] Have you decided?
- Uh...

28
00:01:48,744 --> 00:01:50,955
Uh... [chuckles nervously] Not yet, no.

29
00:01:51,038 --> 00:01:54,542
Is that right?

30
00:01:55,251 --> 00:02:00,131
The Droplet of the Reaper is nice.

31
00:02:00,214 --> 00:02:01,048
Huh?

32
00:02:01,715 --> 00:02:03,968
What is the Droplet of the Reaper?

33
00:02:04,593 --> 00:02:10,057
[Holger] Someday, I hope you find a way

34
00:02:10,141 --> 00:02:14,937
to heal your broken heart.

35
00:02:16,063 --> 00:02:17,106
[Legoshi] Hmm.

36
00:02:24,488 --> 00:02:26,365
[beeping]

37
00:02:26,448 --> 00:02:29,535
ANTI-CRIME CAMPAIGN
LET'S LIVE TOGETHER

38
00:02:29,618 --> 00:02:31,328
[stage staff] That's good.

39
00:02:31,412 --> 00:02:32,496
Need some tape!

40
00:02:38,127 --> 00:02:41,797
This is an emergency. I need to speak
with the Beastar right away.

41
00:02:41,881 --> 00:02:44,758
Huh? Well, I'm afraid he isn't here.

42
00:02:44,842 --> 00:02:47,511
I heard he'd been seen
on the top floor of the police station.

43
00:02:47,595 --> 00:02:51,765
You heard that... I hope you didn't come
out here on account of some silly rumor.

44
00:02:51,891 --> 00:02:53,183
[receptionist chuckles]

45
00:02:53,267 --> 00:02:55,227
Of course not. That was a joke.

46
00:02:55,311 --> 00:02:56,604
Oh, I see.

47
00:02:57,104 --> 00:03:00,149
I was called here
by the Crime Prevention Department.

48
00:03:00,232 --> 00:03:02,067
Then, may I see your identification?

49
00:03:02,902 --> 00:03:05,112
- Is my student ID all right?
- Sure.

50
00:03:07,448 --> 00:03:10,284
Apparently, some big idol
is going to be here.

51
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:11,368
Uh-huh.

52
00:03:11,452 --> 00:03:14,330
She's really popular
with the younger generation, so...

53
00:03:14,413 --> 00:03:15,915
Oh, all set.

54
00:03:15,998 --> 00:03:20,085
- Take elevator E to the 38th floor.
- Thank you very much.

55
00:03:23,213 --> 00:03:26,842
Oh, right. By chance, do you know
how many floors does this building has?

56
00:03:26,926 --> 00:03:28,260
108.

57
00:03:28,344 --> 00:03:30,971
Good luck to anyone
who tries to take the stairs, right?

58
00:03:31,055 --> 00:03:33,641
They'd have to be pretty silly
to attempt something like that.

59
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:36,352
[laughs] They sure would.

60
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:42,816
[panting heavily]

61
00:03:46,862 --> 00:03:48,864
<i>I need to convince the Beastar.</i>

62
00:03:52,868 --> 00:03:55,120
<i>Fifty-five floors to go.</i>

63
00:03:55,829 --> 00:03:57,498
<i>Can I make it on this leg?</i>

64
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:01,210
[panting]

65
00:04:05,923 --> 00:04:08,425
[guard 2] Five! And guess who wins!

66
00:04:08,509 --> 00:04:10,678
- You never called last card, though.
- What?

67
00:04:10,761 --> 00:04:12,346
Third place again, eh? [laughs]

68
00:04:12,429 --> 00:04:14,974
[groans] Can I just win once?

69
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:18,185
[exhales heavily]

70
00:04:18,269 --> 00:04:20,604
<i>Aren't there supposed to be more floors?</i>

71
00:04:24,566 --> 00:04:25,526
[doorknob rattles]

72
00:04:26,694 --> 00:04:28,696
[tense music playing]

73
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:33,826
<i>Got to remember to thank the Shishi-Gumi.</i>

74
00:04:35,286 --> 00:04:36,620
[door unlocks, opens]

75
00:04:46,046 --> 00:04:47,131
- [alarm beeping]
- Huh?

76
00:04:48,841 --> 00:04:50,718
[guard 1] Fire door on 100th?

77
00:04:52,219 --> 00:04:54,013
I'm happy to go give it a look.

78
00:04:54,096 --> 00:04:56,974
- Put the game on pause for now.
- Hey! Come on now.

79
00:05:02,313 --> 00:05:03,647
[Louis] <i>I can go up from here.</i>

80
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:15,367
[music ends]

81
00:05:18,662 --> 00:05:20,622
[whirring]

82
00:05:20,706 --> 00:05:21,749
[dings]

83
00:05:27,421 --> 00:05:29,798
I'm on 100. Everything looks clear.

84
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,676
[guard 3 over radio]
<i>Is the system acting up again?</i>

85
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,844
[guard 2] I'll check.

86
00:05:38,348 --> 00:05:39,391
[door opens]

87
00:05:40,476 --> 00:05:41,643
[door closes]

88
00:05:49,610 --> 00:05:51,820
[suspenseful music plays]

89
00:05:51,904 --> 00:05:52,780
- Huh?
- [gasps]

90
00:05:53,739 --> 00:05:56,450
- Hey! Get back here!
- [door locks]

91
00:05:56,533 --> 00:05:58,702
[grunting]

92
00:06:00,829 --> 00:06:02,206
Open this door!

93
00:06:05,084 --> 00:06:07,294
- Hey! [grunting]
- [doorknob rattling]

94
00:06:09,338 --> 00:06:10,339
[thudding]

95
00:06:12,674 --> 00:06:14,176
[guard 2 grunting]

96
00:06:22,684 --> 00:06:23,519
Huh?

97
00:06:23,602 --> 00:06:25,729
[chuckles]

98
00:06:25,813 --> 00:06:28,607
Time to come out, little fawn.

99
00:06:29,483 --> 00:06:31,360
Huh? Come on!

100
00:06:32,027 --> 00:06:33,403
Where did he go?

101
00:06:37,658 --> 00:06:40,077
[groaning]

102
00:06:45,833 --> 00:06:47,000
Uh...

103
00:06:47,084 --> 00:06:50,879
[guard 2 over radio] <i>Intruder alert!
Be on the lookout for a teenage male deer!</i>

104
00:06:51,672 --> 00:06:52,506
[chuckles]

105
00:06:53,549 --> 00:06:55,217
[sighs wearily]

106
00:06:57,636 --> 00:07:00,139
{\an8}[Gon] A joint drama club?

107
00:07:00,222 --> 00:07:04,268
That's what we'd like you to approve.
Carnivores and herbivores sharing a stage.

108
00:07:04,351 --> 00:07:07,146
Together, we'd rock that meteor festival.

109
00:07:07,229 --> 00:07:08,772
[Gon] I can't approve that.

110
00:07:09,481 --> 00:07:11,942
You two should understand that
better than anyone.

111
00:07:12,443 --> 00:07:14,069
Of course we do.

112
00:07:14,153 --> 00:07:18,115
Last year, our club went through things
nobody should ever have to deal with.

113
00:07:18,657 --> 00:07:20,492
That's why this matters!

114
00:07:20,576 --> 00:07:22,870
{\an8}FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR
REAPPLICATION FORM

115
00:07:22,953 --> 00:07:27,291
{\an8}[Els] This is something we need to do!
Carnivores and herbivores together!

116
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,710
- That's why this matters?
- Yes.

117
00:07:30,377 --> 00:07:31,211
Oh.

118
00:07:31,795 --> 00:07:34,465
So, your plan is to perform
<i>Adler the Reaper</i> then?

119
00:07:35,132 --> 00:07:37,092
- Right.
- But why?

120
00:07:37,593 --> 00:07:39,595
Because it's about love between species,

121
00:07:39,678 --> 00:07:41,930
sacrificing yourself
for those you care about.

122
00:07:42,014 --> 00:07:44,725
And for our drama club,
that's a story that means something!

123
00:07:44,808 --> 00:07:48,061
If you're wondering about casting,
we still haven't locked in our Adler yet.

124
00:07:48,145 --> 00:07:50,689
- But we have time to figure that out--
- Enough, stop already.

125
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,734
Is that truly the message
you want to convey?

126
00:07:54,234 --> 00:07:57,112
That true love justifies
throwing your life away?

127
00:07:57,738 --> 00:07:58,864
- [Bill] Uh...
- [Els] Huh?

128
00:08:00,324 --> 00:08:03,827
After experiencing a devouring incident,
you two surely understand.

129
00:08:04,453 --> 00:08:06,955
Death solves nothing
for those left behind.

130
00:08:07,039 --> 00:08:10,626
True. But <i>Adler's</i> a classic.
For us, it's sort of a tradition--

131
00:08:10,709 --> 00:08:12,085
Well, be that as it may,

132
00:08:12,753 --> 00:08:17,132
a separated curriculum is ultimately safer
for everybody involved.

133
00:08:17,216 --> 00:08:18,467
Is it not?

134
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:19,468
Yeah.

135
00:08:20,219 --> 00:08:21,470
I guess, but...

136
00:08:22,513 --> 00:08:24,556
And do you wish to die as Adler does?

137
00:08:26,141 --> 00:08:28,852
Well, I'd rather not die at all.

138
00:08:29,603 --> 00:08:30,437
[Gon] Hmm.

139
00:08:32,147 --> 00:08:34,900
Even so, you still want
carnivores and herbivores

140
00:08:34,983 --> 00:08:36,652
to work together in this club?

141
00:08:36,735 --> 00:08:37,986
[both] Yes.

142
00:08:39,071 --> 00:08:43,408
Well, why not channel that feeling
into a new play?

143
00:08:43,992 --> 00:08:44,826
[both] What?

144
00:08:45,327 --> 00:08:46,286
I've been thinking,

145
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:49,498
it's high time for the drama club
to have a new signature play.

146
00:08:49,581 --> 00:08:51,375
A fresh, original script.

147
00:08:51,458 --> 00:08:53,710
[both laugh] Yes, sir!

148
00:08:53,794 --> 00:08:54,878
We'll give it a shot!

149
00:08:59,591 --> 00:09:01,134
[guard] Kines is a narcotic?

150
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,554
That one's rich, kiddo.

151
00:09:03,637 --> 00:09:06,473
- I literally just drank one.
- [gasps]

152
00:09:07,099 --> 00:09:08,934
And I'm feeling pretty great!

153
00:09:09,017 --> 00:09:10,769
[grunts, strains]

154
00:09:12,396 --> 00:09:13,480
[Louis] <i>Is he...</i>

155
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,567
What the hell?

156
00:09:18,110 --> 00:09:21,572
- [groaning, straining]
<i>- It's the Kines reaction. This is bad!</i>

157
00:09:21,655 --> 00:09:23,657
[groaning]

158
00:09:26,159 --> 00:09:28,287
- [snarls]
- [grunts]

159
00:09:31,039 --> 00:09:32,291
- [snarls]
- [metal clangs]

160
00:09:33,292 --> 00:09:34,960
[growling]

161
00:09:35,043 --> 00:09:36,878
[straining] <i>Shit!</i>

162
00:09:36,962 --> 00:09:38,964
[both grunting]

163
00:09:43,719 --> 00:09:45,470
[thrilling music playing]

164
00:09:48,307 --> 00:09:50,183
[thudding]

165
00:09:55,647 --> 00:09:58,567
Attempting to eat an herbivore
at a police station is bold,

166
00:09:58,650 --> 00:09:59,985
but it's also very stupid.

167
00:10:00,068 --> 00:10:00,986
[grunts]

168
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,114
You all right?

169
00:10:07,576 --> 00:10:09,369
I take it that you're the Beastar.

170
00:10:12,748 --> 00:10:14,041
Much appreciated.

171
00:10:17,044 --> 00:10:18,045
[Yahya] Hmm.

172
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:21,048
"KINES IS A DRUG"
THE KINES REPORT

173
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,050
This belong to you?

174
00:10:24,509 --> 00:10:25,761
Yes.

175
00:10:25,844 --> 00:10:27,804
Kines is a dangerous beverage.

176
00:10:28,597 --> 00:10:31,391
It seems this security guard
was a frequent partaker.

177
00:10:32,309 --> 00:10:34,353
If we don't stop it being sold,

178
00:10:34,436 --> 00:10:36,772
these incidents
will keep happening everywhere.

179
00:10:36,855 --> 00:10:39,733
That's what you snuck
into a police station like a spy

180
00:10:39,816 --> 00:10:40,776
to tell me?

181
00:10:40,859 --> 00:10:44,696
- Saving me alone doesn't mean anything.
- Hmm.

182
00:10:45,989 --> 00:10:48,033
You can handle this on your own.

183
00:10:48,116 --> 00:10:49,618
But you're Beastar.

184
00:10:49,701 --> 00:10:52,412
You're able to attack the problem
directly at its root!

185
00:10:53,163 --> 00:10:54,164
I need your help!

186
00:10:54,247 --> 00:10:55,499
- [guard pants]
- [gasps]

187
00:10:56,083 --> 00:10:56,917
[Yahya growls]

188
00:10:57,959 --> 00:11:00,629
[all panting]

189
00:11:01,213 --> 00:11:02,964
[host] Let's move on to the photo session.

190
00:11:03,048 --> 00:11:06,259
- [grunts, groans]
- [host] Please stand in the center first.

191
00:11:06,343 --> 00:11:07,719
- [guard panting]
- [idol] All right.

192
00:11:07,803 --> 00:11:10,639
- [camera shutters clicking]
- Everybody, live together!

193
00:11:11,181 --> 00:11:13,517
[both panting, grunting]

194
00:11:15,268 --> 00:11:18,480
[host] Okay, you ready?
Next, please enter from stage right.

195
00:11:19,689 --> 00:11:21,566
- [idol] Live together!
- [grunts]

196
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:24,027
- [grunting]
- [screams, gasps]

197
00:11:24,111 --> 00:11:25,487
[idol pants, whimpers]

198
00:11:26,196 --> 00:11:27,364
[guard 2] Take it easy!

199
00:11:28,073 --> 00:11:29,116
[guard 3] Stop it!

200
00:11:29,199 --> 00:11:31,076
- Now's your moment.
- [male] What's going on?

201
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:32,619
- All right.
- [guard 3] Hold him down!

202
00:11:32,702 --> 00:11:34,579
- [growling]
- [indistinct shouting]

203
00:11:35,163 --> 00:11:36,581
[Louis] It's Kines!

204
00:11:37,582 --> 00:11:39,459
He's under the influence of Kines!

205
00:11:40,168 --> 00:11:41,795
That's what drove him wild.

206
00:11:42,587 --> 00:11:45,132
This security guard
drank one can of Kines,

207
00:11:45,215 --> 00:11:47,926
and it transformed him
into a meat-frenzied beast!

208
00:11:48,009 --> 00:11:50,262
Hey, check it out. Isn't that
The Horns Conglomerate kid?

209
00:11:50,345 --> 00:11:51,513
If not for a stroke of luck,

210
00:11:51,596 --> 00:11:54,391
I only would have left that elevator
in his stomach.

211
00:11:54,975 --> 00:11:59,062
At this very moment, he would be
tearing my flesh, snapping bones.

212
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:03,859
<i>And this is but one such incident
that Kines is responsible for.</i>

213
00:12:04,526 --> 00:12:05,735
<i>Despite all this,</i>

214
00:12:06,236 --> 00:12:09,531
<i>you can purchase Kines anywhere,
and everyone you know is drinking it.</i>

215
00:12:09,614 --> 00:12:12,075
- You're quite the actor, Louis.
<i>- We can't allow this to go on!</i>

216
00:12:12,159 --> 00:12:15,412
The way you shine in that spotlight,
it's like you were born for it.

217
00:12:15,495 --> 00:12:18,123
<i>Everyone, Kines is a narcotic.</i>

218
00:12:18,748 --> 00:12:20,041
Wow, right out with it.

219
00:12:20,876 --> 00:12:24,337
As a matter of fact,
that's why I came to the station today,

220
00:12:24,421 --> 00:12:26,131
to warn the police of the threat it poses.

221
00:12:26,214 --> 00:12:28,508
- You have any proof of that?
- I do.

222
00:12:29,468 --> 00:12:32,262
And I can present my findings
here and now.

223
00:12:32,345 --> 00:12:34,639
"KINES IS A DRUG"
THE KINES REPORT

224
00:12:34,723 --> 00:12:36,183
[fox] Wait, for real?

225
00:12:36,808 --> 00:12:37,893
That's freaky.

226
00:12:37,976 --> 00:12:41,271
[Legoshi typing] "The Droplet...

227
00:12:41,354 --> 00:12:45,901
of the Reaper."

228
00:12:48,028 --> 00:12:50,989
BREATHTAKING VIEW
THE REAPER'S BLOODDROP

229
00:12:51,072 --> 00:12:52,574
<i>That's not what I expected.</i>

230
00:12:53,742 --> 00:12:56,953
<i>Hmm. I guess even Melon
appreciates beautiful things.</i>

231
00:12:57,829 --> 00:12:58,872
[mouse clicking]

232
00:12:58,955 --> 00:13:00,207
<i>Now, where is it?</i>

233
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:02,876
<i>Oh, here we go.</i>

234
00:13:08,215 --> 00:13:11,301
[Ogma] Do you realize the ramifications
of your little stunt?

235
00:13:12,093 --> 00:13:13,220
Take a look at this.

236
00:13:13,303 --> 00:13:14,304
GOLDEN HIND HOLDINGS

237
00:13:14,387 --> 00:13:15,263
It's crashing.

238
00:13:16,306 --> 00:13:19,684
I should not need to remind you
that the company that produces Kines

239
00:13:19,768 --> 00:13:21,478
is owned by Azuki's family.

240
00:13:22,062 --> 00:13:25,690
Still, you chose to charge ahead
without thinking about the consequences.

241
00:13:25,774 --> 00:13:27,609
- But I--
- I'm not finished.

242
00:13:28,235 --> 00:13:30,862
Because you chose to make a show
out of what you've done,

243
00:13:30,946 --> 00:13:34,241
you've turned it into a scandal
for the The Horns Conglomerate.

244
00:13:34,324 --> 00:13:36,368
Have you heard what people are saying?

245
00:13:37,369 --> 00:13:39,704
That you deliberately staged
a carnivore attack

246
00:13:39,788 --> 00:13:41,623
to spread the idea
that Kines is dangerous.

247
00:13:41,706 --> 00:13:44,709
If I know that a crime will occur
and I do nothing about it,

248
00:13:44,793 --> 00:13:46,378
I'm an accomplice too!

249
00:13:46,461 --> 00:13:48,171
You want me to stand by and watch?

250
00:13:48,255 --> 00:13:50,632
[Ogma] I'm talking about
how you went about it.

251
00:13:51,383 --> 00:13:54,678
Consider, for one solitary moment,
Azuki's parents.

252
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:58,431
They just saw their daughter's fiancé
make a spectacle of himself

253
00:13:58,515 --> 00:14:00,141
in far more ways than one.

254
00:14:01,309 --> 00:14:04,604
Is this about my leg?
I never intended to hide it.

255
00:14:05,397 --> 00:14:08,275
[Ogma] Is this some dramatic ploy
to get the wedding called off?

256
00:14:08,358 --> 00:14:09,192
What?

257
00:14:09,859 --> 00:14:13,446
So, what is it, then?
Are you uninterested in women?

258
00:14:14,364 --> 00:14:16,950
Well, that's a fairly significant
change of topic.

259
00:14:18,785 --> 00:14:22,038
I'm simply asking
if it's women in general you dislike or...

260
00:14:22,914 --> 00:14:25,000
if it's just female deer.

261
00:14:25,834 --> 00:14:28,169
Whatever the case, it poses a problem.

262
00:14:28,837 --> 00:14:31,464
[Louis] I think Azuki is
a perfectly wonderful lady.

263
00:14:33,008 --> 00:14:34,050
Do you now?

264
00:14:34,134 --> 00:14:37,512
I had heard that your evening alone
with her came to a rather troubling end.

265
00:14:37,596 --> 00:14:40,390
What's troubling is my father
keeping tabs on my private life.

266
00:14:40,473 --> 00:14:42,017
Who are you even hearing this from?

267
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:45,478
We're talking as president and successor,
not as father and son.

268
00:14:46,771 --> 00:14:47,939
All right, stand up.

269
00:14:53,445 --> 00:14:56,615
From the moment I first bought you
for seven million,

270
00:14:56,698 --> 00:15:00,327
these sorts of business discussions
became inevitable and essential.

271
00:15:00,911 --> 00:15:04,873
Half a million for your horns,
2.5 million for the leg...

272
00:15:04,956 --> 00:15:07,083
That's ten million
standing in front of me.

273
00:15:08,335 --> 00:15:10,086
Take as many detours as you like,

274
00:15:10,795 --> 00:15:13,715
but I raised you to be the heir
to The Horns Conglomerate.

275
00:15:13,798 --> 00:15:14,799
Don't forget that.

276
00:15:18,595 --> 00:15:20,639
[door opens, closes]

277
00:15:28,897 --> 00:15:29,814
[Legoshi] <i>Hmm.</i>

278
00:15:32,651 --> 00:15:34,945
<i>I've passed by here
on my deliveries before,</i>

279
00:15:36,321 --> 00:15:39,783
<i>but how long has it been
since I looked out at the ocean like this?</i>

280
00:15:39,866 --> 00:15:40,867
[inhales deeply]

281
00:15:42,285 --> 00:15:43,620
<i>That reminds me...</i>

282
00:15:43,703 --> 00:15:46,748
<i>God, I really wish
I could have come out here with Haru.</i>

283
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:50,543
[breathes deeply]

284
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:53,129
<i>Though, if she were here next to me,</i>

285
00:15:53,213 --> 00:15:56,174
<i>I'd probably be too focused on her
to even notice the ocean.</i>

286
00:15:56,758 --> 00:15:58,259
<i>I'd probably creep her out.</i>

287
00:15:58,343 --> 00:16:01,805
<i>Still, would have been nice
to talk about life as we took in the view.</i>

288
00:16:02,305 --> 00:16:03,807
<i>We wouldn't even have to talk.</i>

289
00:16:04,307 --> 00:16:06,476
<i>Just having her near would make me happy.</i>

290
00:16:07,727 --> 00:16:09,896
<i>Ah, come to think of it,</i>

291
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:13,066
<i>I've never gone to the beach
with the guys from room 701.</i>

292
00:16:13,149 --> 00:16:15,068
[chuckles] <i>I'd love to swim with them.</i>

293
00:16:15,568 --> 00:16:17,320
<i>We canines really love the water.</i>

294
00:16:18,071 --> 00:16:18,989
<i>Speaking of water,</i>

295
00:16:19,072 --> 00:16:21,783
<i>someday, I hope Mr. Sagwan
will take me out to the open sea</i>

296
00:16:21,866 --> 00:16:23,326
<i>and show me his homeland.</i>

297
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:25,954
<i>And Ms. Seven could come too.</i> [chuckles]

298
00:16:26,037 --> 00:16:27,747
<i>That would be so fun, I swear.</i>

299
00:16:27,831 --> 00:16:30,333
[breathes deeply]

300
00:16:30,417 --> 00:16:33,670
<i>You know, I'm actually
a pretty cheerful guy.</i>

301
00:16:34,504 --> 00:16:38,049
<i>Or maybe I'm becoming more cheerful.</i>

302
00:16:40,427 --> 00:16:42,345
<i>Eighteen years.</i>

303
00:16:43,013 --> 00:16:45,140
<i>They've ended up being pretty fun.</i>

304
00:16:46,182 --> 00:16:47,726
<i>Thanks to everyone around me.</i>

305
00:16:48,977 --> 00:16:49,936
<i>But...</i>

306
00:16:50,979 --> 00:16:52,063
<i>as for Melon,</i>

307
00:16:53,064 --> 00:16:55,483
<i>maybe he's always
watching the ocean alone,</i>

308
00:16:56,985 --> 00:16:59,571
<i>hoping to be understood.</i>

309
00:17:00,864 --> 00:17:04,743
<i>I wonder what goes through his mind
as he looks at the Droplet of the Reaper.</i>

310
00:17:05,869 --> 00:17:09,372
<i>If only he and I
could just talk things over.</i>

311
00:17:10,874 --> 00:17:12,876
<i>And those leaf tattoos of his...</i>

312
00:17:13,710 --> 00:17:15,003
[scoffs]

313
00:17:15,086 --> 00:17:19,132
<i>I doubt he wants to show them off,
but I bet they're pretty.</i>

314
00:17:21,384 --> 00:17:23,261
<i>Holger mentioned he was lonely,</i>

315
00:17:23,845 --> 00:17:26,139
<i>that he is alone.</i>

316
00:17:27,974 --> 00:17:30,935
<i>If only he would talk to me,
even just a little bit,</i>

317
00:17:31,019 --> 00:17:32,562
<i>I'm sure we could come to an--</i>

318
00:17:32,645 --> 00:17:33,646
[gunshot]

319
00:17:35,398 --> 00:17:36,524
[Legoshi groans]

320
00:17:40,653 --> 00:17:41,488
What?

321
00:17:42,113 --> 00:17:44,949
[Melon imitates Holger] "Are you afraid?

322
00:17:46,868 --> 00:17:50,246
Are you anxious?

323
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:53,249
You must feel so alone."

324
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:55,335
[in normal voice] My soul is laid bare!

325
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:58,379
I feel like I'm drowning in darkness!

326
00:18:00,173 --> 00:18:03,843
[imitates Holger]
"You must have always been alone."

327
00:18:05,053 --> 00:18:06,888
[in normal voice] Oh, it's so true!

328
00:18:06,971 --> 00:18:11,226
Nobody, nobody understands me
or the things I've been through!

329
00:18:11,309 --> 00:18:13,144
Huh? What?

330
00:18:14,229 --> 00:18:17,649
That close to what you thought
I said in that tattoo parlor?

331
00:18:19,109 --> 00:18:21,027
Oh, thank you! How about this?

332
00:18:21,111 --> 00:18:24,656
You can become the one who finally
cracks my code and understands!

333
00:18:24,739 --> 00:18:26,825
- [gasps in disbelief]
- [laughs maniacally]

334
00:18:26,908 --> 00:18:31,496
Alas. The boy with the leopard mother
and gazelle father is a tragic hero.

335
00:18:31,579 --> 00:18:34,582
A life bereft of love
was his ultimate downfall!

336
00:18:34,666 --> 00:18:37,752
Unable to fully trust the friendly wolf
who tried to believe in him,

337
00:18:37,836 --> 00:18:41,464
our hero ended up killing him
with his very own hands!

338
00:18:41,548 --> 00:18:42,757
Bang!

339
00:18:42,841 --> 00:18:44,467
Oh my, what a tragedy.

340
00:18:45,176 --> 00:18:49,013
Oh, yeah, I have, like,
freakily, abnormally good hearing,

341
00:18:49,097 --> 00:18:53,101
so I picked up on your attempts
to follow me right from the get-go.

342
00:18:53,852 --> 00:18:57,522
Though, I got to admit, the fact that
you're still alive did surprise me.

343
00:18:58,189 --> 00:19:00,191
[Legoshi] <i>It was all a trap!</i>

344
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,902
[suspenseful music playing]

345
00:19:08,158 --> 00:19:12,036
Well, anyway, this little reunion
really is a second chance.

346
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,622
This time, I'll make
extra special sure you die.

347
00:19:15,290 --> 00:19:17,584
So, will you be smashed
upon the jagged rocks

348
00:19:17,667 --> 00:19:19,002
till your body is in bits,

349
00:19:19,085 --> 00:19:21,671
or will your lungs fill
as you drown in the ocean?

350
00:19:21,754 --> 00:19:22,797
[softly] Huh.

351
00:19:24,382 --> 00:19:25,717
But why?

352
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,010
[mutters mockingly]

353
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:28,636
All I wanted...

354
00:19:29,596 --> 00:19:32,515
- I just wanted us to talk.
- [laughs maniacally]

355
00:19:33,391 --> 00:19:35,685
Oh, my God, you're killing me here!

356
00:19:35,768 --> 00:19:39,022
[mockingly] "It's just... I wanted to talk,
for us to be friends."

357
00:19:39,105 --> 00:19:41,649
[laughs] God damn it, you're hilarious!

358
00:19:42,275 --> 00:19:45,236
You sympathized with me
and thought I'd sympathize with you.

359
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:50,283
Oh my, you really do live
in a fantasy world, don't you, wolfy boy?

360
00:19:50,366 --> 00:19:52,118
Why are you doing this?

361
00:19:52,827 --> 00:19:54,871
- [snarls]
- [choking]

362
00:19:54,954 --> 00:19:56,831
Just because it's fun.

363
00:19:56,915 --> 00:19:59,667
How can it not be
when someone so full of hope like you

364
00:19:59,751 --> 00:20:02,587
falls right into the death grip
of despair?

365
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:04,172
Thing is, sympathy is boring.

366
00:20:04,255 --> 00:20:07,508
If you want to touch my heart,
there's only one thing you can do.

367
00:20:07,592 --> 00:20:10,011
When you die,
try to make it messy, would ya?

368
00:20:10,094 --> 00:20:13,348
- It's far more entertaining.
- [choking, grunting]

369
00:20:14,766 --> 00:20:15,808
Scary, huh?

370
00:20:16,476 --> 00:20:19,562
Do you want to know
what my favorite thing in the world is?

371
00:20:19,646 --> 00:20:21,314
[choking]

372
00:20:21,397 --> 00:20:24,817
- The face of someone afraid of death.
- [choking, gasping]

373
00:20:24,901 --> 00:20:30,073
No matter what species they are,
everybody makes the same one without fail.

374
00:20:30,156 --> 00:20:34,494
Not a lie to be found,
a face that's genuinely honest.

375
00:20:34,577 --> 00:20:35,745
[strained] Melon.

376
00:20:36,496 --> 00:20:39,332
[Melon laughs maniacally]
Yes, that's the one!

377
00:20:39,916 --> 00:20:43,419
- That face there.
- [choking]

378
00:20:44,087 --> 00:20:45,380
- [Melon] Oh, oh!
- [Legoshi gasps]

379
00:20:56,557 --> 00:20:58,142
[exhales heavily]

380
00:21:00,353 --> 00:21:02,814
The Droplet of the Reaper, huh?

381
00:21:05,358 --> 00:21:06,693
[sighs]

382
00:21:10,321 --> 00:21:11,572
Better get back to it.

383
00:21:14,826 --> 00:21:16,619
[muffled grunting]

384
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:22,583
[muffled groaning]

385
00:21:25,628 --> 00:21:26,754
[Melon in distance] Correct!

386
00:21:26,838 --> 00:21:30,216
The concept of meat as we know it
only came into being after the war.

387
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:32,260
- [Haru sighs]
- [Melon] The war changed everything.

388
00:21:32,343 --> 00:21:34,137
[continues indistinctly]

389
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,014
He still hasn't gotten back to you?

390
00:21:36,097 --> 00:21:38,433
You should break up with him
already, Haru.

391
00:21:38,516 --> 00:21:42,687
- [sighs] Maybe I should.
- There are so many nice guys out there.

392
00:21:42,770 --> 00:21:45,148
- You'll find one in no time.
- [Melon clears throat] You two!

393
00:21:45,231 --> 00:21:46,190
[both gasp]

394
00:21:46,274 --> 00:21:48,651
- Done chatting?
- I'm sorry.

395
00:21:49,694 --> 00:21:50,611
As I was saying,

396
00:21:50,695 --> 00:21:54,032
the relationship between these two groups
began to break down.

397
00:21:54,615 --> 00:21:57,076
They stood on the line
between love and hate.

398
00:21:57,160 --> 00:22:00,246
From there,
complicated emotions began to emerge.

399
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

400
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,834
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

401
00:22:04,917 --> 00:22:08,338
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

402
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,467
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

403
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,803
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

404
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

405
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,561
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

406
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

407
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,569
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

408
00:22:32,612 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

409
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

410
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,791
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

411
00:22:44,874 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

412
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,044
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

413
00:22:48,127 --> 00:22:52,590
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

414
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

415
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,765
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

416
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,767
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

417
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,268
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

418
00:23:04,894 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

419
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

420
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,652
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

421
00:23:13,444 --> 00:23:16,322
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

422
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

423
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,372
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

424
00:23:25,373 --> 00:23:28,876
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
